{
  "_comment": [
    "Shared vectors for the glide of a ContextMenu: a finger that opened the menu with a long",
    "press keeps moving, the row under it highlights, and lifting chooses it",
    "(CoreContextMenuContract.defaultGlideSlop / exceedsGlideSlop and CoreContextMenuGlide).",
    "Read by coui_core (the slop, the hit-test rule, and every trace replayed on the state",
    "machine over a synthesized layout), coui_flutter (every trace is replayed on a real",
    "ContextMenu as pointer events: the long-press recogniser opens the menu and the glide",
    "follows the same pointer), coui_web (every trace is replayed on the press tracker with a",
    "manual clock) and a real-Chrome probe (the same traces as touch events on the compiled",
    "component). A change on one platform fails the others.",
    "",
    "Coordinates and times. A trace's first event is a 'down' at (x, y) in px, relative to the",
    "top-left of the region that carries the menu. The menu opens 500 ms later (the hold is the",
    "long-press table's), flush at that point. 'at' is ms since the down; every later event is",
    "applied once the clock has reached it, and the menu has finished mounting by the first one.",
    "",
    "Where a later pointer event lands ('to') is written against the menu, not in pixels, so the",
    "same trace is true of any layout: {offset: [dx, dy]} is relative to the point the menu opened",
    "at; {row: i, at: [fx, fy]} is a fraction of interactive row i's box where the list has it, in",
    "view or not (rows are the action, checkbox and radio items, counted from 0 in item order,",
    "disabled ones included; labels, dividers and gaps are not rows); {between: [i, j]} is the",
    "middle of the space between interactive rows i and j; {outside: side, by: n} is n px past the",
    "panel's edge, centred on it; {same: true} is where the pointer already was.",
    "",
    "What each event leaves behind ('expect', every key optional): 'highlight' is the interactive",
    "row that is lit, or null; 'cues' is how many selection ticks have played since the down;",
    "'open' is whether the menu is still open; 'activated' is every row that was activated, in",
    "order. Activating an action row closes the menu, as a tap on it does; activating a checkbox or",
    "a radio row does not (toggling keeps the menu open).",
    "",
    "A trace may say 'glide': false (the default is true - the widget's glideToSelect), 'haptics':",
    "true (default false), and 'menu' (a key of 'menus'; default 'basic'). 'platforms' names who",
    "replays it (absent: all). The scroll event moves the list so that interactive row N is the",
    "first one in view.",
    "",
    "'layout' is only what the Core test needs to turn the symbolic positions into pixels; the",
    "seats measure their own menus. 'hits' is the pure hit-test rule over given boxes and is read",
    "by the Core test alone."
  ],
  "slop": 18,
